    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** (83.29) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (77.82) anchor the Austin Waves lineup as our primary offensive catalysts. **Gunnar Henderson** benefits significantly from a favorable matchup against Bailey Ober, whose xERA of 4.78 and high-volume delivery create a perfect environment for him to exploit the stolen base category, further boosted by an elite top-of-the-order position. Meanwhile, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** draws a strong platoon advantage against Patrick Sandoval, with the park factor and his high base projection making him our most reliable run producer. **Luis Robert Jr.** also warrants high confidence (75.66) as he faces the southpaw Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez, where his dynamic platoon advantage provides a substantial lift to his efficiency score, helping us chase those critical power categories.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Sam Antonacci** in the lineup over **Nasim Nunez**. While **Sam Antonacci** carries a lower score of 46.86 due to a suboptimal L/L matchup against Nick Lodolo and a lower batting order spot, his presence in the outfield is currently prioritized for his positional floor. **Nasim Nunez** (49.65) was the strongest bench candidate, nearly displacing the bottom of our order; however, he was edged out due to Shota Imanaga\u2019s solid 3.75 xERA and the negative impact of his lower batting order slot, which constrained his potential for high-leverage production. We are also monitoring the lineup status of **Liam Hicks** and **Drake Baldwin** closely; although both are projected at decent efficiency, the \"Lineup Pending\" tag introduces risk regarding their respective placements in the order. Owners should watch for any late-afternoon lineup swaps, particularly concerning **Coby Mayo**, whose score is highly sensitive to his position in the batting order against the vulnerable Bailey Ober.",
